 # SolverBuilder wiring: boundary types, zone labels, surface properties, film coefficients
 **Review ID**: coredeep-10
 **Category**: core-deep
-**Date**: 2026-05-25
+**Date**: 2026-05-26
 
 ## Files Reviewed
 crates/hares-core/src/dwelling/solver_builder.rs
 

[0m
Review complete. Findings written to `docs/reviews/core-deep/coredeep-10-solver-builder-wiring.md`.

**Summary**: 7 findings (0 critical, 1 high, 3 medium, 3 low).

The high-severity finding is the **zone-type-only indexing** in `boundary_zone_index()` and `find_zone_idx()` — both use `position()` which returns only the first matching zone, so multi-unit buildings (duplexes, etc.) with multiple conditioned zones will have all surfaces incorrectly aggregated into the first thermal node.

The medium findings cover silent fallbacks for missing/unrecognised zone types mapped to outdoor/zone-0, and Door/Other boundaries being invisible in diagnostics despite participating in the thermal model.

The film coefficient implementation is per-surface (not global) and correctly separates convection-only interior resistance (ASHRAE Simple/TARP) from radiative coupling handled via star-mesh or ScriptF, as documented in the code.
